From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: back every fresh guest commit of a host page or more

0148 offered the host only fresh RW commits of at least 1 MiB. Kingdom Come's census (0149) showed that most of its ordinary guest memory is RW views filled by commits under 1 MiB (8.7 GiB in 112,232 commits by load end, about 80 KiB each), so offer every fresh RW commit in the window that holds a whole host page. The rules are otherwise 0148's: only plain VirtualAlloc views, never write-watched, exec, guard or write-copy pages, only commits with no page already committed, the host-page remainder at either end stays ordinary, detach to ordinary memory before any protection other than RW, and every range Wine stops using is reported.

Tens of thousands of small backed ranges would make 0148's interval table (a linear scan on every unmap, decommit and protection change) too slow, so track backed pages in a bitmap over the window instead: one bit per 16 KiB page of [0x7000000000, 0x7c00000000), 384 KiB of zero-fill BSS. A release looks only at the pages of its own range, and reports each run of backed pages, at most 64 MiB at a time (a detach copies that much through a temporary buffer). Portable host tests check marking, clearing, runs and clipping against a page model.

Class: host-app
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-14-donor-pool-widen.md
Offered-upstream: no; optional iOS host experiment
